<section class="in-hero"><div class="in-w in-hero-g"><div class="in-hero-t"><p class="in-mono">// a guide to deeper learning</p><h1>Don&rsquo;t just<br>remember it.<br><mark>Understand it.</mark></h1><p class="in-lead">Insight is a free study guide about thinking well. Build questions that climb from recall to real understanding, then test whether you can explain an idea simply enough for anyone to follow.</p>
<div class="in-hero-a"><a class="in-btn" href="#bloom">Build better questions</a><a class="in-btn in-btn-o" href="#explain">Test my explanation</a></div></div>
<div class="in-hero-v"><figure class="in-hi1"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1775682131334-bd22b17f57f1?auto=format&fit=crop&w=520&h=640&q=75" alt="a glowing light bulb with colourful reflections" width="520" height="640" fetchpriority="high"></figure><figure class="in-hi2"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1769776399293-e75896444616?auto=format&fit=crop&w=300&h=300&q=75" alt="a white light bulb standing out from two blue ones" width="300" height="300" fetchpriority="high"></figure><div class="in-note"><span class="in-mono">aha!</span><b>moment</b><i></i></div><svg class="in-spark" viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M50 4v24M50 72v24M4 50h24M72 50h24M17 17l17 17M66 66l17 17M83 17L66 34M34 66L17 83"/></svg></div></div>
<div class="in-w in-stats stg"><p class="rv"><b data-count="6">0</b><span>levels of thinking</span></p><p class="rv"><b data-count="4">0</b><span>steps to the Feynman technique</span></p><p class="rv"><b data-count="2">0</b><span>free tools</span></p><p class="rv"><b data-count="0">0</b><span>accounts needed</span></p></div></section>

<section class="in-s in-bl" id="bloom"><div class="in-w"><div class="in-sh"><span class="in-num">01</span><div><p class="in-mono">tool / question builder</p><h2 class="rv">Bloom&rsquo;s question builder</h2><p class="in-p">Questions at different levels make you think in different ways. Type a topic, choose a level on the pyramid and get question starters you can use to quiz yourself or a study group.</p></div></div>
<div class="in-bl-g"><div class="in-bl-v"><svg viewBox="0 0 400 340" class="in-pyr" aria-hidden="false"><g class="lvl" data-v="5" tabindex="0" role="button" aria-label="Create"><path d="M180 20 H220 L250 72 H150 Z" fill="#FF6B5B"/><text x="200" y="52">Create</text></g><g class="lvl" data-v="4" tabindex="0" role="button" aria-label="Evaluate"><path d="M150 72 H250 L280 124 H120 Z" fill="#FF9F45"/><text x="200" y="104">Evaluate</text></g><g class="lvl" data-v="3" tabindex="0" role="button" aria-label="Analyse"><path d="M120 124 H280 L310 176 H90 Z" fill="#FFE14D"/><text x="200" y="156">Analyse</text></g><g class="lvl" data-v="2" tabindex="0" role="button" aria-label="Apply"><path d="M90 176 H310 L340 228 H60 Z" fill="#7BD88F"/><text x="200" y="208">Apply</text></g><g class="lvl" data-v="1" tabindex="0" role="button" aria-label="Understand"><path d="M60 228 H340 L370 280 H30 Z" fill="#4CC9F0"/><text x="200" y="260">Understand</text></g><g class="lvl" data-v="0" tabindex="0" role="button" aria-label="Remember"><path d="M30 280 H370 L400 332 H0 Z" fill="#8E7DFF"/><text x="200" y="312">Remember</text></g></svg><figure class="in-bl-i"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1758270705482-cee87ea98738?auto=format&fit=crop&w=520&h=220&q=75" alt="students talking in a lecture hall" width="520" height="220" loading="lazy"></figure></div><div class="in-panel"><label class="in-lb" for="bl-t">Your topic</label><input type="text" id="bl-t" class="in-in" value="photosynthesis" maxlength="50"><div aria-live="polite"><p class="in-lvl"><span id="bl-n">Level 2</span><b id="bl-l">Understand</b></p><p class="in-p" id="bl-d"></p><ol class="in-qs" id="bl-q"></ol></div><button type="button" class="in-btn in-btn-s" id="bl-c">Copy questions</button><span class="in-mono in-copied" id="bl-ok" aria-live="polite"></span></div></div></div></section>

<section class="in-s in-ex" id="explain"><div class="in-w"><div class="in-sh"><span class="in-num">02</span><div><p class="in-mono">tool / explanation tester</p><h2 class="rv">The Feynman explanation tester</h2><p class="in-p">Write an explanation as if teaching a twelve-year-old. We measure how readable it is, highlight long words and long sentences, and suggest where to simplify. Nothing you type leaves your browser.</p></div></div>
<div class="in-ex-g"><div><label class="in-lb" for="ex-t">Your explanation</label><textarea id="ex-t" class="in-ta" rows="9">Photosynthesis is how plants make their own food. They take in sunlight, water from the soil and carbon dioxide from the air. Inside their leaves, tiny green parts use the energy of light to turn these into sugar, which the plant uses to grow. Oxygen is released as a by-product, which is the oxygen we breathe.</textarea><div class="in-hl" id="ex-hl" aria-hidden="true"></div></div>
<div class="in-ex-r" aria-live="polite"><div class="in-gauge"><svg viewBox="0 0 200 110" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 100a80 80 0 0 1 160 0" class="g0"/><path d="M20 100a80 80 0 0 1 160 0" class="g1" id="ex-arc"/></svg><b id="ex-g">Grade 7</b><span id="ex-gl">reading level</span></div><dl class="in-ex-s"><div><dt>Words</dt><dd id="ex-w"></dd></div><div><dt>Avg. sentence</dt><dd id="ex-s"></dd></div><div><dt>Long words</dt><dd id="ex-l"></dd></div></dl><p class="in-verdict" id="ex-v"></p><figure class="in-ex-i"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1590103514966-5e2a11c13e21?auto=format&fit=crop&w=520&h=220&q=75" alt="a person writing on a whiteboard" width="520" height="220" loading="lazy"></figure></div></div></div></section>

<section class="in-s in-hab"><div class="in-w"><div class="in-sh"><span class="in-num">03</span><div><p class="in-mono">habits</p><h2 class="rv">Four habits of curious learners</h2></div></div><ol class="in-hbs"><li class="in-hb rv"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1697301439916-169bd6844842?auto=format&fit=crop&w=400&h=300&q=75" alt="a magnifying glass resting on an open book" width="400" height="300" loading="lazy"></figure><span class="in-mono">01</span><b>Read closely</b><p>Slow down and question the text.</p></li><li class="in-hb rv"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1758876022649-ab858801c6dc?auto=format&fit=crop&w=400&h=300&q=75" alt="a woman thinking with a pen at her desk" width="400" height="300" loading="lazy"></figure><span class="in-mono">02</span><b>Pause to think</b><p>Ask what you already know.</p></li><li class="in-hb rv"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1758876201723-9f050343325c?auto=format&fit=crop&w=400&h=300&q=75" alt="a woman looking at sticky notes on a wall" width="400" height="300" loading="lazy"></figure><span class="in-mono">03</span><b>Map connections</b><p>Lay ideas out where you can see them.</p></li><li class="in-hb rv"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1637094408647-0d81d08f81b5?auto=format&fit=crop&w=400&h=300&q=75" alt="a person holding two pieces of a puzzle" width="400" height="300" loading="lazy"></figure><span class="in-mono">04</span><b>Fit the pieces</b><p>Link new ideas to old ones.</p></li></ol></div></section>

<section class="in-gd"><div class="in-w in-gd-g"><a class="in-gc rv" href="blooms-taxonomy-guide.html"><span class="in-mono">guide 01 &rarr;</span><b>Bloom&rsquo;s Taxonomy, Explained</b><p>Six levels of thinking, from remembering to creating, and how to use them when you study.</p></a><a class="in-gc in-gc2 rv" href="feynman-technique-guide.html"><span class="in-mono">guide 02 &rarr;</span><b>The Feynman Technique</b><p>Learn anything by explaining it simply, spotting the gaps and filling them.</p></a></div></section>

